@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`createRentalService` keeps equipment in a `Map` and bookings in an array with numeric `from`/`to`. `book` already checks overlap with `from < b.to && b.from < to`, and `parseMidnight` validates periods.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Reuse the existing period validation and overlap rule so `availability` and `book` always agree.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Pricing in results, returning full equipment objects, cancellations.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Add `availability(query: AvailabilityQuery): string[]` to `RentalService`, with `AvailabilityQuery { start; end; kind?: EquipmentKind }`.
+- Validate dates with `parseMidnight` and `to > from`; validate `kind` when not `undefined`. Assumption: an unknown kind throws (consistent with `addEquipment`) rather than returning empty.
+- Filter items by kind and absence of overlapping bookings, then sort ids with a plain default `.sort()` (code-unit order, deterministic).
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+Linear scan over items and bookings; fine at desk scale.
